# Wave W17-Z (Route 215): puddle turf — rain-slick turf, puddle-polish flecks: a deep walked green carrying bright polish flecks where the story’s rain has slicked the grass to a shine, meteor country’s wet apron (design: rain-slick grass all the way to Shardfall’s gate — the rain is a story biome in the design, not a weather field; the polish is drawn in the kind, no rain register invented). Route 215’s own ground — split from its twin Route 214 by wetness entire (the wet meteor road vs the dry meadow) and from Farewell Spring’s meadow by traffic: this grass is rained on and walked, that one is sat beside.
